  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective Labour administration systems and efficient workplace inspection in place</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Weak enforcement and outdated labour laws and occupational safety and health (OSH) standards in Sri Lanka leave many workers exposed to unsafe conditions and labour rights violations, particularly in the informal economy. Current OSH legislation covers only about 30 per cent of the workforce, while limited inspection capacity and gaps in addressing modern workplace risks further undermine worker protection.

The ILO works to strengthen labour inspection systems and modernize OSH regulations to ensure safer workplaces, prevent occupational injuries and illnesses, and uphold workers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; rights. These efforts protect workers, support employers through clearer safety standards, and help the government meet international labour commitments. Implementation is carried out in partnership with the Department of Labour, employers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; and workers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations, and relevant ministries.</narrative>
  </description>
